# B.9.3 Main Models: Englishness (Continuous) {#sec-b8-engl}

The Englishness Economic DV models replicate the Britishness structure with Englishness as the identity moderator, following the same logic as Appendix B.3. For unemployment and claimant indicators, the Englishness interaction is present but somewhat attenuated relative to Britishness, consistent with the pattern documented for `immigSelf`. For local income, as in Appendix B.3, the Englishness interaction reveals a small but discernible conditional structure absent in the Britishness models, suggesting that Englishness captures a distinct channel through which constituency-level economic context shapes Economic immigration attitudes.

## B.9.3.1 Local Unemployment Rate {#sec-b8-engl-unemp}

Baseline specifications show no significant unconditional unemployment effect. The interaction models reveal a positive and highly significant unemployment main effect (β ≈ 0.036, p \< 0.001), a non-significant Englishness main effect, and a negative and highly significant interaction term (β ≈ −0.006, p \< 0.001), robust to age controls. This mirrors the directional structure observed in the Britishness unemployment models and indicates that higher local unemployment is associated with more permissive economic immigration attitudes at the highest levels of Englishness, with the association attenuating as Englishness decreases. The interaction is larger in magnitude than its Britishness counterpart, suggesting Englishness more strongly structures this conditional relationship for the economic DV.

```{r b8-engl-unemp-main}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Unemp only"    = m_u0.1_eng,
    "(2) + Englishness" = m_u1_eng,
    "(3) Unemp + Age"   = m_u0.2_eng,
    "(4) + Englishness" = m_u2_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", unemployment_rate = "Unemp. rate (local)", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.13. Local Unemployment Rate and Economic Immigration Attitudes: Main Effects (Englishness)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigEcon.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

```{r b8-engl-unemp-int}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Interaction"       = m_u3_eng,
    "(2) Interaction + Age" = m_u4_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", unemployment_rate = "Unemp. rate (local)",
                  "engl:unemployment_rate" = "Englishness × Unemp. rate", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.14. Local Unemployment Rate × Englishness: Interaction Models (Economic DV)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigEcon.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

## B.9.3.2 Claimant Count {#sec-b8-engl-claimant}

Main-effect specifications show a small positive unconditional claimant association (β ≈ 0.010–0.011, p \< 0.05), consistent across age-controlled and uncontrolled specifications. The interaction models yield a negative and significant Englishness main effect (β ≈ −0.031 to −0.032, p \< 0.001), a positive and significant claimant main effect (β ≈ 0.016–0.017, p \< 0.01), but a non-significant interaction term (β ≈ −0.001, p \> 0.1) in both specifications. As with the Britishness claimant result in B.9.1.2, there is no evidence of conditional moderation by Englishness for the claimant indicator with the economic immigration DV.

```{r b8-engl-claimant-main}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Claimant only"  = m_c0.1_eng,
    "(2) + Englishness"  = m_c1_eng,
    "(3) Claimant + Age" = m_c0.2_eng,
    "(4) + Englishness"  = m_c2_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", claimant_rate = "Claimant count (local)", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.15. Claimant Count and Economic Immigration Attitudes: Main Effects (Englishness)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigEcon.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

```{r b8-engl-claimant-int}
