  list(
    "(1) Interaction"       = m_c3_eng,
    "(2) Interaction + Age" = m_c4_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", claimant_rate = "Claimant count (local)",
                  "engl:claimant_rate" = "Englishness × Claimant count", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.16. Claimant Count × Englishness: Interaction Models (Economic DV)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigEcon.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

## B.9.3.3 Local Income (ASHE) {#sec-b8-engl-income}

Main-effect specifications show no significant unconditional income association. The interaction models, however, reveal a positive and significant income main effect (β ≈ 0.000, p \< 0.001), a positive and significant Englishness main effect (β ≈ 0.024–0.025, p \< 0.05), and a negative and highly significant interaction term (β ≈ −0.000, p \< 0.001), robust to age controls. This parallels the Britishness income result in B.9.1.3 and indicates that higher local earnings are associated with more permissive economic immigration attitudes among respondents with weaker Englishness, with the association attenuating as Englishness increases.

```{r b8-engl-income-main}
